{"id": "sfusd-e-rate-inflated-equipment", "title": "Four E-Rate bids rose by $26.1 million while four San Francisco schools dropped out", "seconds": 80.9, "voice": "elevenlabs:9PVP7ENhDskL0KYHAKtD", "narrator": "Jerry B.", "made": "2026-11-26", "key": "0189825b896cae92", "words": 225, "beats": [{"scene": "bid", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "San Francisco schools applied for federal E-Rate support for communications equipment.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 4.32, "shot": "r0", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "plea", "kicker": "U.S. District Court, Northern District of California", "text": "E-Rate program", "mark": "E-Rate program"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.8, 1.19, 1.54, 1.68, 2.02, 2.41, 2.81, 2.95, 3.68]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "hook", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "The application covered 46 schools, down from 50.", "t0": 4.44, "t1": 7.63, "shot": "r1", "visual": {"type": "hook", "words": ["What", "changed", "between", "bid", "and", "application?"], "sub": "San Francisco schools"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.79, 1.12, 1.7, 2.34, 2.59, 2.78]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "record", "ref": ["suspicious[0]", "established[2]"], "text": "Even with fewer schools, the amounts submitted on four items exceeded the bids by $26,105,745.", "t0": 7.75, "t1": 14.21, "shot": "r2", "visual": {"type": "record", "layout": "amounts", "context": "Four items on the application", "heading": "Bids compared with the submission", "source": "plea", "rows": [{"icon": "file", "label": "Four bids", "value": "$62,153,768"}, {"icon": "file", "label": "Submitted amounts", "value": "$88,259,513"}]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.46, 0.76, 1.52, 1.66, 1.98, 2.43, 2.57, 2.87, 3.18, 3.63, 3.76, 4.09, 4.25, 4.52, 5.16, 5.47, 5.69, 6.03]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "Sales representatives for an equipment maker advised schools and helped select vendors.", "t0": 14.33, "t1": 18.25, "shot": "r3", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "plea", "kicker": "U.S. District Court, Northern District of California", "text": "Vendor referrals", "mark": "Vendor referrals"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.37, 1.02, 1.17, 1.26, 1.67, 2.0, 2.38, 2.77, 2.91, 3.13, 3.48]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1]", "established[3]"], "text": "Inter-Tel admitted helping disguise ineligible videoconferencing equipment in the application.", "t0": 18.37, "t1": 22.93, "shot": "r4", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Ineligible equipment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.57, 0.95, 1.25, 1.76, 2.31, 3.18, 3.61, 3.7, 3.83]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "The funding administrator approved data, cabling and telephone exchanges. It rejected the server request.", "t0": 23.05, "t1": 28.84, "shot": "r5", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "plea", "kicker": "U.S. District Court, Northern District of California", "text": "Funding decision", "mark": "Funding decision"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 1.11, 1.51, 1.99, 2.45, 2.55, 3.02, 4.08, 4.3, 4.78, 4.91, 5.24]}, {"scene": "bid", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[4]"], "text": "Inter-Tel learned that the prices exceeded the bids. It did not tell the administrator.", "t0": 28.96, "t1": 33.36, "shot": "r6", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Submitted prices"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.6, 0.84, 0.97, 1.08, 1.54, 1.97, 2.09, 2.85, 3.05, 3.24, 3.43, 3.64, 3.75]}, {"scene": "funding", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[0]"], "text": "The administrator committed $48.68 million across the two providers’ applications.", "t0": 33.58, "t1": 38.83, "shot": "r7", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "congress", "kicker": "U.S. House Committee on Energy and Commerce", "text": "District investigation", "mark": "District investigation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.79, 1.23, 1.77, 2.07, 2.38, 2.6, 2.98, 3.35, 3.7, 3.8, 4.01, 4.5]}, {"scene": "funding", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[0]"], "text": "Superintendent Arlene Ackerman declined the funding and alerted the FBI.", "t0": 38.95, "t1": 43.07, "shot": "r8", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "District response"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.83, 1.23, 1.67, 2.09, 2.18, 2.65, 2.87, 3.29, 3.46]}, {"scene": "funding", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[3]", "established[0]"], "text": "The commitment was not a payment to the district.", "t0": 43.19, "t1": 45.27, "shot": "r9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Commitment and payment"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.59, 0.77, 0.95, 1.03, 1.39, 1.51, 1.62]}, {"scene": "funding", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[5]"], "text": "Inter-Tel’s civil settlement specified how to divide seven million dollars.", "t0": 45.39, "t1": 49.43, "shot": "r10", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "settle", "kicker": "U.S. Department of Justice and SFUSD", "text": "Federal settlement", "mark": "Federal settlement"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.62, 0.93, 1.37, 2.01, 2.16, 2.28, 2.8, 3.21, 3.57]}, {"scene": "funding", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2]", "established[5]"], "text": "After the specified payment, the district was due 21 percent, or 1.47 million dollars.", "t0": 49.55, "t1": 55.62, "shot": "r11", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$1.47 million", "label": "San Francisco’s agreed whistleblower share"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.3, 0.41, 1.04, 1.7, 1.89, 2.28, 2.47, 2.71, 3.24, 4.01, 4.28, 4.49, 4.77, 5.02, 5.34, 5.65]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "The FCC barred Inter-Tel from E-Rate for one year after its 2005 convictions.", "t0": 55.84, "t1": 60.63, "shot": "r12", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "fcc", "kicker": "Federal Communications Commission", "text": "Inter-Tel debarment order", "mark": "Inter-Tel debarment order"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.78, 1.08, 1.58, 1.79, 2.11, 2.31, 2.54, 2.8, 3.09, 3.24, 3.45, 3.85, 4.13]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["established[6]"], "text": "It also ordered audits during the first two funding periods after Inter-Tel returned.", "t0": 60.75, "t1": 64.58, "shot": "r13", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Review after re-entry"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.44, 0.73, 1.04, 1.29, 1.4, 1.65, 1.86, 2.23, 2.65, 2.93, 3.36]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The FCC described NEC’s separate plan to charge a proposed workstation donation to the program.", "t0": 64.7, "t1": 69.92, "shot": "r14", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "nec", "kicker": "Federal Communications Commission", "text": "Proposed donation", "mark": "Proposed donation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.78, 1.29, 1.81, 2.19, 2.54, 2.66, 2.94, 3.01, 3.45, 4.02, 4.49, 4.6, 4.7]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "doc", "ref": ["established[1]"], "text": "The Commission imposed a separate six-month bar on NEC.", "t0": 70.04, "t1": 73.05, "shot": "r15", "visual": {"type": "doc", "source": "nec", "kicker": "Federal Communications Commission", "text": "Separate debarment order", "mark": "Separate debarment order"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.53, 0.98, 1.07, 1.46, 2.0, 2.28, 2.43]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The agreement sets the district’s share. The sources do not confirm when it received payment.", "t0": 73.17, "t1": 77.76, "shot": "r16", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["District receipt", "Actual loss"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.58, 0.84, 0.96, 1.38, 2.11, 2.29, 2.69, 2.88, 3.06, 3.59, 3.75, 3.85, 4.21]}, {"scene": "orders", "kind": "end", "ref": ["status"], "text": "Every source is linked in the case file below.", "t0": 77.88, "t1": 79.99, "shot": "r17", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.32, 0.63, 0.79, 1.03, 1.11, 1.21, 1.47, 1.75]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"bid": "What happened to the bids?", "funding": "What did the district receive?", "orders": "Two providers, two orders"}, "look": "dossier", "hook": "document"}